{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents","id":965355,"title":"Akira-styled Exigents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-07T17:22:32-07:00","id":965355,"title":"Akira-styled Exigents?","content":"I was wondering something: I'm looking for Exalted-types that get their powers from Akira-type psionic/psychic power, suitably charged-up and changed for fantasy. To anyone who knows: Is this likely to be a splat at some point? Because for some reason, I really, really like the idea of high-blast psychic types in fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:46:19-07:00","id":965433,"title":"","content":"Infernals using the charms of She Who Lives in Her Name were able to use telekinesis, mind reading, and the like. That might be something to look into if you are interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:00:07-07:00","id":965464,"title":"","content":"Yep, 2E Infernal SWLiHN Charms include a psionic blast, mind-reading, mind-controlling people whose minds you destroyed with psionic blasting, and lots of telekinesis. And what could maybe be called telekinetic healing if you squint.<br /> Infernal Adorjan Charms also let you get telepathy, for the tiny price of becoming mute. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But outside of SWLiHN's large telekinetic Charm tree, there haven't been any canon Exalted types with dedicated psionics-focused Charmsets.<br /> <br /> I have no clue whether any of the new Exalted types will have such a thing in 3E, but what we last saw about Infernals suggests that they will have far, far fewer psionics in 3E.<br /> <br /> <br /> I suspect that mind-reading is going to remain very rare and difficult in Exalted. In 2E both Solars and Infernals have easy-to-use, flawless lie-detection Charms, and the Solar version got a nerf for 3E so that it doesn't cut off whole avenues of storytelling. While 2E Infernals and Sidereals each have one limited mind-reading Charm, I imagine that any 3E mind-reading would have to remain both weak and rare to avoid it becoming the next Judge's Ear Technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-08-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:05:29-07:00","id":965466,"title":"","content":"Ironically I tried making Psionic powered Exalts in 2.5e.<br /> <br /> I stopped because... well I'd be making things in 2.5e. I never got beyond the beginning of the brainstorming phase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:19:39-07:00","id":965497,"title":"","content":"without stats I'd make a late-stage Akira as some kind of Autochtonian techno-horror built by or created by or just being an apostate alchemical of some kind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:43:08-07:00","id":965506,"title":"","content":"It could be neat to see the Defiler Caste handled as its own exalt type where Mind Hand doesn't need to play second fiddle to the options of the castes with a bigger focus on combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T22:59:54-07:00","id":965511,"title":"","content":"No thank you. I love Defilers as Infernals from Hell. That's what I've wanted to play for all these years. I've never gotten the appeal of separating Infernals from their origins in Hell and turning them into Exigents or Green Solars. If you don't want to play an Infernal from Hell ... you don't have to.<br /> <br /> A more psionics-focused Exalt could easily be an Exigent, but that's no reason to gut Infernals of an entire Caste's concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would a psionics-focused Exigent make more sense as Attribute-based, or Ability-based? I feel like it makes more aesthetic sense to start with each Attribute and expand psionic applications from them. Something like:<br /> <br /> INT: manipulating abstract and intangible energies -- life-force, Essence, Wyld; Sorcery initiation Charms<br /> PER: clairsentience, Essence-sight<br /> WIT: ??<br /> CHR: empathy<br /> MAN: telepathy<br /> DEX: telekinesis<br /> STR: ... also telekinesis? or psionic blasting as literal physical blasting?<br /> STA: using psionic force in self-defense and physical self-enhancement","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-08-2016, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:58:26-07:00","id":965603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965511#post965511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No thank you. I love Defilers as Infernals from Hell. That's what I've wanted to play for all these years. I've never gotten the appeal of separating Infernals from their origins in Hell and turning them into Exigents or Green Solars. If you don't want to play an Infernal from Hell ... you don't have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played Infernals, I enjoy Infernals, my avatar is one of my Infernals and the Storyteller of my Infernals game contributed towards several of the charms you mentioned so please don't make this about me not liking Infernals.<br /> <br /> I suggested using a Defiler as the basis of an Exigent. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-08-2016, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T05:05:09-07:00","id":965608,"title":"","content":"Not this argument again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:25:34-07:00","id":965694,"title":"","content":"Sorry I misunderstood, it looked like you meant take Defilers completely <i><b>out</b></i> of Infernals and make them a separate splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:35:03-07:00","id":965800,"title":"","content":"Do I detect Eleven and Mob somewhere behind this topic thread? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (because they've got me thinking more than I have for a while about how psionic heroes are actually cool.).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965511#post965511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a psionics-focused Exigent make more sense as Attribute-based, or Ability-based? I feel like it makes more aesthetic sense to start with each Attribute and expand psionic applications from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in either case they could work. Like, if you have Abilities, then you can have psy-Medicine and psy-Archery and psy-Stealth, etc, and there aren't any particular areas of the Ability map that I think can't be convincingly psyd up (behold: psy-Bureuacracy!).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, either Ability or Attribute also feels a bit weird because I don't usually think of psychic powers like, &quot;There's a guy who's really good at moving skillfully, therefore it's an extension of his power to move things dexterously by his mind&quot;. Psychic powers in fiction seem usually a gift that happens without reference to normal Abilities or Attributes, not a complement or intensifier of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:12:22-07:00","id":965823,"title":"","content":"Psionics are really neat. I love them myself and some of my favorite characters are psionics (I am playing one in a D&amp;D game right now) but they come with a lot of cultural baggage attached. I have to wonder if they're particularly &quot;in-theme&quot; for the Swords and Sandal's ideal that Exalted has - and to be fair this is an issue that psionics often struggle with in other RPG lines like Dungeons and Dragons.<br /> <br /> Is there a way to take the basic concept of psionics but repackage it in a way that doesn't make it grate against the basic mood of Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:55:02-07:00","id":965852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965823#post965823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to take the basic concept of psionics but repackage it in a way that doesn't make it grate against the basic mood of Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm running into that hurdle myself.<br /> <br /> To be honest, the idea of psionics in Exalted is a really tricky ground to walk, as one does not naturally intertwine with the other. She Who Lives in Her Name managed to pull off some of those tricks (see the Defiler charm set, obviously), but only as a handful of effects in a greater tree. Further, Mind-Hand Manipulation deliberately simulates and evokes telekinesis, but I don\u2019t quite recall anything else in her arsenal that does the same for telepathy, telemetry, or the like. <br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but grouping all those abilities together really feels like a very modern take on psychic powers. As such, what really gets me is wondering from what kind of deity (or deities) would be the patron(s) of such an Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:11:47-07:00","id":965861,"title":"","content":"Honestly I find making charm ideas for psionics easy as hell. I mean if you go out and brainstorm, you'll find a TON of different ideas you can experiment with psychic powers alone. Honestly making an entirely new Exalt type complete with different castes is easily done as there is a ton of space.<br /> <br /> The only challenges I find are:<br /> <br /> 1) Effort<br /> 2) Figuring out their proper power tier. This would help explain balance their charm power. I'd place them at Celestial/Sidereal level, but I'm biased as I know Celestials very well compared to Dragonblooded.<br /> 3) Figuring out their spot. What can they do compared to a Defiler? Remember SWL uses Psychic power not because she's a yozi of psychic power, but rather she's a bunch of floating orbs and using psychic power is the most efficient way to accomplish things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:14:22-07:00","id":965863,"title":"","content":"Creating/weilding a blade with your mind sounds like something an aestic could do, or a god of ritual combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:22:10-07:00","id":965868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965800#post965800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I detect Eleven and Mob somewhere behind this topic thread? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (because they've got me thinking more than I have for a while about how psionic heroes are actually cool.).</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and I remember a piece of artwork for Exalted 3 (before the book was released) that was supposed to be a portrait of different Exalt-types. One of the guys there was, like, clutching his head and there appeared to be a green snake thing (?) popping out of his head, aura-style. And it left me wondering if they were going to have psychic-style exalts in the game. <br /> <br /> I wonder if you could tie them to some fantasy Land of Dreams for the setting-flavor....Anyway, just a thought. Good to see there are others who are at least interested in the idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:28:39-07:00","id":965869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965863#post965863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating/weilding a blade with your mind sounds like something an aestic could do, or a god of ritual combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gold standard for cool Psionic powers has to be Psi-Ops for the PS2/Xbox. Some of the things they do with the psychic powers of the game and how well they implemented them made it an extremely solid game.<br /> <br /> Too bad the company died before making a sequel.<br /> <br /> Ironically Mewtwo from pokemon is another choice for pure telekinetic power. In his second movie he moved an entire island by himself and resisted a brainwashing drone so well that Giovanni said that Mewtwo would destroy his own body before his mind gave up. Which just goes to show both the mental and psionic might he had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:35:54-07:00","id":965876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965823#post965823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psionics are really neat. I love them myself and some of my favorite characters are psionics (I am playing one in a D&amp;D game right now) but they come with a lot of cultural baggage attached. I have to wonder if they're particularly &quot;in-theme&quot; for the Swords and Sandal's ideal that Exalted has - and to be fair this is an issue that psionics often struggle with in other RPG lines like Dungeons and Dragons.<br /> <br /> Is there a way to take the basic concept of psionics but repackage it in a way that doesn't make it grate against the basic mood of Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI agree, although I also think something like the Elfen Lied semi-tangible arms was a decent middle ground.<br /> <br /> I do have to wonder if association with psionics is necessarily worth tying directly to She Who Lives in Her Name again. Certainly, I would like some things to move a bit away from the ultra-rational supercomputer idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:53:40-07:00","id":965885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965823#post965823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to take the basic concept of psionics but repackage it in a way that doesn't make it grate against the basic mood of Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, thinking about this, what if we changed the angle slightly?<br /> <br /> In this case, play it up as spiritual enlightenment. In many fables and folk stories based out of nations like India or China, gurus, hermits, and mystics were capable of performing all manner of supernatural powers thanks to their efforts to attain enlightenment. Stories included mystics being able to float, being able to read minds, see into the future, being able to telekinetically move objects and perform all manner of feats commonly associated with &quot;psionic powers.&quot;<br /> <br /> An Exigent (or other character) built off this idea, that being an &quot;enlightened mystic&quot; can also bring spiritual powers, could probably have an array of abilities that are highly reminiscent of the kind of psionic abilities you see in movies, games and anime, yet at the same time still fits within the themes and moods of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T15:06:55-07:00","id":965893,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Anubis on a related note I was just about to post this when I saw your post:<br /> <br /> Psionic powers and psychokinesis culturally have a lot of references to science - and that's the aspect by which they tend to come up with She Who Lives In Her Name, like to do with the supremacy of the rational intellect over reality - but alternately also to &quot;Age of Aquarius&quot; type mysticism that is rooted in concepts like Exalted draws on for the mystical essence driven powers that Exalts have. Think more like psychic shamans or (this sounds horrible but I can't think of a better way to say it) hippies who've owned their &quot;Third Eye&quot; than Psi Corps. <br /> <br /> Though that style of psychic is maybe not very Akira, and is maybe still kind of modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T16:23:57-07:00","id":965914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965885#post965885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, thinking about this, what if we changed the angle slightly?<br /> <br /> In this case, play it up as spiritual enlightenment. In many fables and folk stories based out of nations like India or China, gurus, hermits, and mystics were capable of performing all manner of supernatural powers thanks to their efforts to attain enlightenment. Stories included mystics being able to float, being able to read minds, see into the future, being able to telekinetically move objects and perform all manner of feats commonly associated with &quot;psionic powers.&quot;<br /> <br /> An Exigent (or other character) built off this idea, that being an &quot;enlightened mystic&quot; can also bring spiritual powers, could probably have an array of abilities that are highly reminiscent of the kind of psionic abilities you see in movies, games and anime, yet at the same time still fits within the themes and moods of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if we're in Exalted and feel beholden to the caste system (maybe we shouldn't), we could have two right there: one caste that uses methods of Enlightenment to achieve their abilities, and one that uses ecstatic methods (drugs/herbs, ritualized pain, etc.) I keep thinking of the Ahl-I-Batini and Mount Qaf from Mage: Ascension, except what if it was tapped into by the Cult of Ecstasy or the Taftani? Think of an &quot;ocean of dreams&quot; from which these Exalted-types draw their energy: wild, turbulent, ever-changing. So you either go with the flow, or you harness it by harnessing yourself. <br /> <br /> I'd use Ability-based Charms, myself, and re-skin certain ones to get the feel of achieving the humanly improbable/impossible in a psychic sort of way. Mild mind-bending, telekinesis, telemetry, internal alchemy, seeing spirits. Maybe have a specialized Sorcery adapted to achieve the really high-end stuff. They'd most likely be Celestial, but I could see them being at the level of Dragon-Blooded with special Charms to get power boosts by working in unison. <br /> <br /> As always, just some thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:22:10-07:00","id":965964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965885#post965885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, play it up as spiritual enlightenment. In many fables and folk stories based out of nations like India or China, gurus, hermits, and mystics were capable of performing all manner of supernatural powers thanks to their efforts to attain enlightenment. Stories included mystics being able to float, being able to read minds, see into the future, being able to telekinetically move objects and perform all manner of feats commonly associated with &quot;psionic powers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI find this compatible with my current interest in Infernals aligning with a lot of weird yogi narratives as a contrast to Solar folk hero narratives.<br /> <br /> It may not specifically be related to the central conceit of Green Sun Princes as denied, rebuked, or ruined by the world, but a link can be drawn.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:03:32-07:00","id":966007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/965355-akira-styled-exigents?p=965876#post965876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have to wonder if association with psionics is necessarily worth tying directly to She Who Lives in Her Name again. Certainly, I would like some things to move a bit away from the ultra-rational supercomputer idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can do far more with the will-crushing power of her true name now that 2e social combat and keyword implementation don't push that towards easily dismissed parlour tricks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}